@startuml "Command - Menu (GoF) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title GoF's own example — Design Patterns, pp. 233-242

package "before the pattern" {
  class "problem.MenuItem" as Naive {
    - label : String
    - application : Application
    + clicked()
  }
  note bottom of Naive
    The toolkit's menu item imports the
    application and branches on its label.
    <b>Every new menu entry edits the toolkit.</b>
  end note
}

package "after it" {
  class Menu
  class "solution.MenuItem" as Item <<Invoker>> {
    - command : Command
    + clicked()
    + setCommand(Command)
  }
  interface Command <<Command>> {
    + execute()
  }
  class PasteCommand <<ConcreteCommand>>
  class OpenCommand <<ConcreteCommand>>
  class MacroCommand <<ConcreteCommand>> {
    + add(Command)
    + remove(Command)
  }
  class "SimpleCommand<R>" as Simple <<ConcreteCommand>> {
    - receiver : R
    - action : Consumer<R>
  }
  class Document <<Receiver>> {
    + open()
    + copy()
    + paste()
  }
  class Application <<Receiver, Client>> {
    + add(Document)
  }

  Menu o--> "*" Item
  Item o--> "command" Command
  Command <|.. PasteCommand
  Command <|.. OpenCommand
  Command <|.. MacroCommand
  Command <|.. Simple
  MacroCommand o--> "*" Command
  PasteCommand --> Document
  OpenCommand --> Application
}

Naive -[hidden]right- Menu

note right of Simple
  GoF's C++ template. In Java the
  member-function pointer is a method
  reference: Document::paste
end note
@enduml
